## User preferences

- When planning, the user said “tôi và bạn sẽ duyệt từng phần để hoàn thiện plan trước” -> work section-by-section; do not finalize or edit later sections or the shared document until explicitly approved. [Task 1]
- The user required “3 demo theo 1 flow chứ k rời rạc” -> use one connected case narrative with handoff and state continuity, not unrelated feature demonstrations. [Task 1]
- For team sharing, the user requested concise selected-option summaries and an online document -> preserve separate artifact boundaries and write to the shared document only after approval. [Task 1]

## Reusable knowledge

- The official FAQ checked in this rollout requires building on 31/10/2026 during 10:00–17:00 and excludes pre-built code/existing projects. Treat scope/design by 19/10 and preparation-ready by 25/10 as preparation, with implementation/integration/testing on event day. [Task 1]
- Approved flow: `DH001` splits shirt into shipment A and hat into B; one case `CS001` spans CS A then CS B. Demo 1 records a missing-hat complaint while B is in transit; Demo 2 links the new conversation after B is delivered; Demo 3 keeps old/new evidence distinct and requires CS approval before an operations investigation is executed and recorded. [Task 1]
- Use one role-based web app (Customer and CS) with persistent cases, conversations, messages, evidence, orders, shipments, assignees, and action history. AI proposes links/drafts/actions; CS confirms linking and approves sending/escalation; backend records actual result. Distinguish customer claims, system facts, and unverified conclusions. [Task 1]
- Selected stack: Next.js + TypeScript, Tailwind CSS + shadcn/ui, Supabase PostgreSQL/Storage, OpenAI SDK + Responses API, Zod, Vercel, and a local fallback. MVP tools are backend function tools (`find_cases`, `get_case_context`, `get_order_shipments`): model requests, backend validates identity/arguments and queries Supabase, then returns `function_call_output` using matching `call_id`; no MCP server is needed. [Task 1]
